1
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:09,500
Hold on a second.

2
00:00:14,010 --> 00:00:15,110
I can't wait.

3
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:17,070
Because I'm your boyfriend.

4
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:19,860
So I can do whatever I want, right?

5
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:29,760
Give me a second.

6
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:36,860
Just take that off for now.

7
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,450
Can you put mine on instead?

8
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:48,750
Oh...

9
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:51,180
Um...

10
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:22,940
Thank you.

11
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:25,980
Yeah.

12
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:28,460
Um...

13
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:34,240
I'm sorry.

14
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:36,240
It's fine.

15
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:38,180
I'm not mad.

16
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:41,860
But we aren't just friends anymore.

17
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,560
We're a couple.

18
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:49,330
You need to start acting like it.

19
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:52,140
Okay.

20
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:04,940
Why is the door locked?

21
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:14,060
Watarai, what are you
doing? It's time to hit the baths.

22
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:15,260
Oh, sorry.

23
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:18,050
Huh?

24
00:02:18,090 --> 00:02:19,090
Hioki?

25
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:21,760
What's going on?

26
00:02:23,470 --> 00:02:24,470
Nothing.

27
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:26,440
I was just lending Hioki some clothes.

28
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:29,500
Ah, found you guys.

29
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:30,660
What are you up to?

30
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,180
Oh, Hioki, you're here too.

31
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:34,270
Oh, yeah, nothing much.

32
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:37,100
Hioki, your face is super red.

33
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:38,840
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

34
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:41,480
By the way, Tsujitani was
looking for you earlier.

35
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:43,030
Said dinner's almost ready.

36
00:02:43,110 --> 00:02:44,660
Right, I should head over.

37
00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:46,236
I'll bring your jacket back later.

38
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:47,260
Don't worry about it.

39
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:48,920
I'm fine with just a T-shirt.

40
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:51,960
All right.

41
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:54,520
I'll see you guys later.

42
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:56,340
Yeah.

43
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:07,000
"School Trip: Joined a Group I'm Not Close to Season2"

44
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:09,436
(Study Camp Episode 2) So,
what was that all about earlier?

45
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:10,660
Something definitely happened.

46
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:12,700
Not really.

47
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,220
It's just...

48
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:17,740
What?

49
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:19,140
Did Hioki do something wrong?

50
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:22,750
No, Hioki didn't do anything wrong at all.

51
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:25,780
It's just...

52
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:27,880
It's my own issue.

53
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:37,700
I think...

54
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,340
My feelings for Hioki...

55
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:42,950
run way deeper than he realizes.

56
00:04:52,610 --> 00:04:53,780
Man...

57
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:55,480
I'm beat.

58
00:04:57,620 --> 00:04:59,050
All that's left to do now is sleep.

59
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:04,480
Good evening.

60
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:07,460
- We're borrowing Hioki for a bit.
- Pardon the intrusion.

61
00:05:10,130 --> 00:05:11,460
Hioki.

62
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:13,670
Slide the door open.

63
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:16,380
- A little further. - Okay.

64
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,020
All right, we're here.

65
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:20,240
This is the place.

66
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:21,720
Watarai's here too.

67
00:05:22,930 --> 00:05:23,990
I'm here too, you know.

68
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:26,480
What's going on?

69
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,930
We wanted to all sleep together
like we did on the school trip.

70
00:05:30,350 --> 00:05:34,000
We took a shot and asked the teacher,
and they actually let us switch rooms.

71
00:05:34,570 --> 00:05:35,480
Seriously?

72
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:36,500
Yeah.

73
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:40,280
This was already a five-person room, so
after talking it over with the roommates,

74
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,820
they agreed to trade with us.

75
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:43,380
Told you, didn't I?

76
00:05:43,860 --> 00:05:45,130
Said I'd figure something out.

77
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:54,120
Even though I was the one
who actually negotiated it.

78
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:56,690
Hey, it was my idea in the first place!

79
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,440
Huh? What, you wanna go?

80
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,720
Hold on, don't fight.

81
00:06:00,940 --> 00:06:02,130
Bring it on!

82
00:06:02,470 --> 00:06:04,470
Oh, you really went there.

83
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:08,560
Hioki, help me out here.

84
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:41,020
Oh, you went and got your glasses.

85
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,200
Oh, yeah.

86
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,760
Want something to drink?

87
00:06:46,130 --> 00:06:47,140
Are you sure?

88
00:06:47,660 --> 00:06:48,660
Yeah.

89
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:54,080
Keep it a secret from Watarai, though.

90
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:57,140
He gets super intense
whenever it comes to you.

91
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:59,120
Here.

92
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:05,100
Thanks.

93
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:17,100
Can I ask you something?

94
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,200
Does Watarai ever say anything to you guys?

95
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:27,920
Like if something's bothering
him, or anything about me...

96
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,080
Well...

97
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:35,880
Ever since we got put in different
classes, he's seemed pretty lonely.

98
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:37,530
What about you?

99
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:39,060
Huh?

100
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,930
Don't you get lonely?

101
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:44,840
Well...

102
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:48,230
It's not like I don't.

103
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:52,320
If I had to guess,

104
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:55,940
I think Watarai...

105
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:58,680
just wants you to rely
on him a little more.

106
00:08:03,130 --> 00:08:04,130
Man...

107
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,420
This really takes me back.

108
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:09,550
Yeah, I know what you mean.

109
00:08:09,710 --> 00:08:11,760
The school trip was such a blast.

110
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:13,380
Even though a lot went down.

111
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,280
Oh, yeah.

112
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:17,280
Like when Hioki got lost
at the amusement park.

113
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,520
Oh, the lost child incident?

114
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:22,770
Actually, Hioki probably doesn't
know this, but right before you got lost,

115
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,336
things got super awkward
between us and those girls.

116
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:26,440
Oh, right, that did happen.

117
00:08:26,580 --> 00:08:29,110
Yeah, the girls were
totally jealous of Hioki.

118
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:30,650
Huh?

119
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:33,330
Watarai-kun, what do you even...

120
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:36,120
like about Hioki-kun anyway?

121
00:08:39,030 --> 00:08:40,040
Everything.

122
00:08:40,920 --> 00:08:41,920
Huh?

123
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:43,410
You actually said that?

124
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,120
Yeah.

125
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:47,680
More or less.

126
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:54,640
Speaking of Hioki, there was also the
glasses thing and the morning sun incident.

127
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,390
What's the morning sun incident?

128
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:02,420
Everyone was talking about how pretty the
morning sun, 'asahi', was, and Hioki suddenly...

129
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:04,220
Oh...

130
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:07,717
Got all embarrassed
because his name is Asahi too!

131
00:09:07,741 --> 00:09:08,619
Right!

132
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:09,620
That totally happened.

133
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:10,700
Oh, that.

134
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:12,779
Just forget about that already.

135
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:14,610
Who cares? It was cute.

136
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:15,570
Right?

137
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:16,600
Yeah.

138
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,300
It really was cute.

139
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:24,200
And then there was the haunted house.

140
00:09:26,493 --> 00:09:28,113
- The mummy incident?
- Yeah!

141
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,376
That was seriously hilarious.

142
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:31,080
- So funny.
- That's the one, right?

143
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:34,020
Hioki mistook the
mummy's hand for Watarai's,

144
00:09:34,050 --> 00:09:36,260
went 'Huh?' and just
screamed his head off.

145
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,480
- He screamed so loud!
- Right?

146
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:40,840
- You were pretty bad yourself!
- Seriously!

147
00:09:41,010 --> 00:09:42,099
You were the most scared out of all of us.

148
00:09:42,100 --> 00:09:44,600
(Kameyama Onsen Hotel)

149
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,500
He's out like a light.

150
00:10:10,540 --> 00:10:11,920
You're still up?

151
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:12,940
Yeah.

152
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,260
Being here with you...

153
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:18,120
probably put his mind
at ease so he could sleep.

154
00:10:21,966 --> 00:10:23,900
Looks like you were spot on, Nakasato.

155
00:10:25,140 --> 00:10:26,140
Huh?

156
00:10:27,390 --> 00:10:28,390
I...

157
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:33,860
had no idea at all...

158
00:10:34,770 --> 00:10:36,850
just how insecure Watarai was feeling.

159
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:42,060
I get it.

160
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:44,320
I used to be the exact same way.

161
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:46,660
Huh?

162
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:51,060
Remember how I mentioned
my ex-girlfriend on the school trip?

163
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:55,640
Nakasato was dating his
childhood friend up until recently.

164
00:10:55,710 --> 00:10:57,270
Then some guy swooped in and stole her.

165
00:10:58,040 --> 00:10:59,540
Her college-student tutor.

166
00:11:01,710 --> 00:11:02,710
Oh, right.

167
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:05,940
I'll never forgive her
for cheating, of course.

168
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:10,100
But sometimes I can't help wondering...

169
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:14,780
Back then...

170
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:17,140
if we'd just been able to talk openly...

171
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:20,290
about our worries and frustrations,

172
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,360
maybe things would've
turned out differently.

173
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:30,160
Even when you're a couple,

174
00:11:30,910 --> 00:11:33,310
they can't read your mind if
you keep everything bottled up.

175
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:43,060
Shoot, I should sleep. Good night.

176
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:44,600
Good night.

177
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,080
Hioki...

178
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:18,140
Watarai.

179
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Watarai.

180
00:12:24,630 --> 00:12:25,660
Watarai, wake up.

181
00:12:30,710 --> 00:12:31,730
Hioki?

182
00:12:39,620 --> 00:12:42,500
What's wrong? Can't sleep?

183
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:43,640
No.

184
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:45,340
I just...

185
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,020
wanted to do something
before everyone else wakes up.

186
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:08,220
Here.

187
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,280
Let's eat this together.

188
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,540
Breakfast.

189
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:13,500
Huh?

190
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:15,280
Didn't you say it before we left?

191
00:13:16,793 --> 00:13:18,080
I can't wait.

192
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:19,580
Riding the bus with Hioki.

193
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:20,840
Eating meals with Hioki.

194
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:23,660
Taking a bath with Hioki.

195
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:27,520
We couldn't ride the bus
or take a bath together,

196
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:30,600
so I figured we could
at least share a meal.

197
00:13:34,860 --> 00:13:35,990
You remembered that?

198
00:13:37,140 --> 00:13:38,140
Yeah.

199
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:39,500
After all, technically I am...

200
00:13:40,950 --> 00:13:42,050
your boyfriend.

201
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:45,140
What do you mean, 'technically'?

202
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:47,770
You're my real, actual boyfriend.

203
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,100
Yeah.

204
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:50,160
But you see,

205
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:52,380
since I...

206
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:54,940
have never dated anyone before,

207
00:13:55,170 --> 00:13:58,440
I'm still kind of a newbie at this.

208
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:00,480
Um...

209
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:04,360
I feel like I don't express
my feelings well enough.

210
00:14:06,930 --> 00:14:07,930
Truth is,

211
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:12,180
I like you way more
than you think, Watarai.

212
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:19,160
Now that we're seniors, being in a
classroom without you really is lonely.

213
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,949
I find myself wishing
break time would never end,

214
00:14:21,950 --> 00:14:24,739
or that I didn't have club practice
so I could spend more time with you.

215
00:14:24,740 --> 00:14:25,740
Things like that.

216
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:28,240
Before I know it,

217
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:30,720
that's all I'm ever thinking about.

218
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:34,560
Um...

219
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:38,270
I'm usually too shy

220
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,400
to actually say it out loud, though.

221
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:45,380
I really like you,

222
00:14:45,550 --> 00:14:46,550
Watarai.

223
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,200
Hold on...

224
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:57,320
I can't help it...

225
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:00,260
You just made me way too happy.

226
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:04,020
Yeah.

227
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:06,020
Someone might walk by, though.

228
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,120
So, um...

229
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:09,960
let's stop here for now.

230
00:15:12,250 --> 00:15:13,250
Okay.

231
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:35,700
Watch your step.

232
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:41,780
The morning sun
really is beautiful.

233
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:45,660
Yeah.

234
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:48,660
Sorry.

235
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:50,970
Hearing "Asahi" makes
you embarrassed, right?

236
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:52,980
No, it's totally fine.

237
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:54,416
That one time was just a fluke.

238
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:57,060
I'm usually pretty immune
to "the morning sun."

239
00:15:58,480 --> 00:15:59,480
Is that so?

240
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,460
Well then...

241
00:16:06,820 --> 00:16:07,820
I love you,

242
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:09,720
Asahi.

243
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:16,160
Hold on.

244
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:18,740
To that kind of "Asahi,"...

245
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,040
I haven't built up an immunity yet.

246
00:16:21,890 --> 00:16:23,060
What does that even mean?

247
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:26,830
And how can you be immune
to the morning sun anyway?

248
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:30,990
Anyway, let's just eat.

249
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,490
Okay.

250
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:36,280
- Thanks for the food.
- Let's eat.

251
00:16:47,170 --> 00:16:49,500
By the way, how much longer
do you have club activities?

252
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:52,436
Things will wrap up for me
after this month's tournament.

253
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:53,460
And just like that,

254
00:16:53,980 --> 00:16:57,020
our study camp came to an end.

255
00:16:57,260 --> 00:16:58,260
Hioki.

256
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:01,450
- Let's walk home together.
- Sure.

257
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,520
Thanks.

258
00:17:13,070 --> 00:17:14,070
And then,

259
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:17,340
the day I'd been waiting
for finally arrived...

260
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:21,660
Hioki.

261
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:25,540
My first date with
Watarai in a while, and...

262
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:27,060
Have you been waiting long?

263
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:28,240
Not at all, I just got here.

264
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:31,360
Ta-da!

265
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:32,880
Huh?

266
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:35,250
Happy birthday.

267
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:37,320
...my birthday.

268
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,720
Thank you.

269
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:41,020
You actually remembered.

270
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:42,360
Of course I did.

271
00:17:42,666 --> 00:17:43,906
I am your boyfriend, after all.

272
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:50,400
It'll be a pain to carry around,
though, so I'll hold onto it for now.

273
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:51,636
No, it's fine. I can carry it.

274
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:52,660
Don't worry about it.

275
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:53,940
Let's go.

276
00:17:54,020 --> 00:17:55,220
Whatever you want to do today,

277
00:17:56,110 --> 00:17:57,190
we're doing it all.

278
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:03,050
Come to think of it, I haven't
been to the zoo in ages.

279
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,360
Same here.

280
00:18:04,361 --> 00:18:05,870
What animals do you want to see?

281
00:18:17,360 --> 00:18:18,520
Whoa, it's coming over here.

282
00:18:18,620 --> 00:18:19,630
It's huge.

283
00:18:21,930 --> 00:18:22,930
So long!

284
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,010
That's crazy, it's super long.

285
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:27,720
Alright, say cheese.

286
00:18:31,440 --> 00:18:32,230
Whoa, amazing.

287
00:18:32,260 --> 00:18:34,860
- So cool.
- Here you go. Is it good?

288
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,230
So cute.

289
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,900
Why are you petting of me?

290
00:18:38,120 --> 00:18:39,920
Because both you and
the alpaca are adorable.

291
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,320
So cute.

292
00:18:43,020 --> 00:18:44,300
They're all looking right at us.

293
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:47,240
A giraffe.

294
00:18:47,410 --> 00:18:49,080
- What do you think?
- Yeah, it's cute.

295
00:18:49,740 --> 00:18:51,120
This is nice.

296
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:55,020
This one's really cute. It
looks just like you, Hioki.

297
00:18:55,170 --> 00:18:56,170
Does it?

298
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:57,380
Spitting image.

299
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:05,800
It's cute, sure, but so are you.

300
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:10,070
- Let's eat.
- Digging in.

301
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,759
This is delicious.

302
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:18,480
You've got some whipped cream on your face.

303
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:25,980
There, all gone.

304
00:19:26,940 --> 00:19:27,940
Thanks.

305
00:19:33,906 --> 00:19:34,676
Hioki.

306
00:19:34,910 --> 00:19:35,660
Hmm?

307
00:19:35,910 --> 00:19:37,230
I want to say it to you properly.

308
00:19:37,670 --> 00:19:38,840
Happy birthday.

309
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:43,560
Thank you.

310
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:47,280
There are two? Why?

311
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:49,660
One for this year, and one for last year.

312
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:53,850
Your birthday passed before we got
close last year, so I missed my chance.

313
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:58,940
Hair oil and a belt?

314
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:02,400
I can use both for school! Can I open them?

315
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:03,460
Yeah, go ahead.

316
00:20:09,650 --> 00:20:11,110
If you use them every day,

317
00:20:12,700 --> 00:20:13,780
it'll make me really happy.

318
00:20:14,620 --> 00:20:17,080
Then I definitely have
to use them every day.

319
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:18,520
Yeah.

320
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:20,440
Thank you.

321
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:24,140
Is this scent okay for you?

322
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,220
Yeah, it's great.

323
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:29,540
I really like it.

324
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,200
Yeah.

325
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:35,520
I like it, too.

326
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:43,860
Hioki.

327
00:20:44,150 --> 00:20:45,150
Hmm?

328
00:20:46,560 --> 00:20:47,790
Here's to us,

329
00:20:49,030 --> 00:20:50,030
as your boyfriend.

330
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:55,700
Yeah.

331
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Right back at you.

332
00:20:57,720 --> 00:20:59,240
Here's to us.

333
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:01,220
To us.

334
00:21:08,460 --> 00:21:09,460
Thanks.

335
00:21:11,010 --> 00:21:12,300
I'm so glad you like it.

336
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:15,230
- It's super cute.
- Right? I knew it'd look good on you.

337
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:20,220
The first day of being eighteen.

338
00:21:21,890 --> 00:21:25,170
Celebrating my birthday with a
partner for the first time in my life...

339
00:21:25,230 --> 00:21:28,440
made me happier than I
ever could've imagined.

340
00:21:55,170 --> 00:21:56,776
(Thank you for today, I had the best time.)

341
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:59,250
(I love you so much.)

342
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:06,300
However,

343
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,160
at the time, it never
even crossed my mind...

344
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:14,020
Huh? Tsukasa?

345
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:21,500
that for Watarai,

346
00:22:21,900 --> 00:22:24,380
(I love you the most too.
Let's stay together forever.)

347
00:22:29,460 --> 00:22:33,580
this wasn't his first relationship.

348
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:42,060
Suzu?

349
00:22:49,930 --> 00:22:50,930
(Next Episode Preview)

350
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:52,290
(A secret meeting with his ex-girlfriend?!)
Watarai!

351
00:22:52,310 --> 00:22:53,560
Are you serious?!

352
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:57,000
(Feeling jealous for the first time—) What
were Watarai's past relationships like?

353
00:22:57,040 --> 00:23:00,820
Friend or not, cheating is
the one thing I'll never forgive.

354
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:03,180
We need to talk.

355
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:04,880
Am I getting dumped?

356
00:23:07,490 --> 00:23:08,430
Don't do this...

357
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:09,590
Tsujitani.
